#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059731 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059544 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8bff08bf-0035-5f05-9607-493b301e8717" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given Two Perpendicular Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "dfc10727-c0d7-5b83-a4f6-afe3eb4831cd" :question/math-academy-id "e-4324" :question/problem "Let $[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ t\\end{aligned}]$. Given that $\\mathbf{a} \\perp \\mathbf{b}$, find the value of $t$." :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\mathbf{a} \\perp \\mathbf{b}$ ($\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are perpendicular) if and only if $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-2)+(-2)\\cdot 5+1\\cdot t \\\\  & =-8-10+t \\\\  & =t-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ t-18 & =0 \\\\ t & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8bff08bf-0035-5f05-9607-493b301e8717" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048187} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050938}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497696 :question-generator/id #uuid "8810f20e-2e11-504b-9733-0c8d213d16f4" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186059731.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060184 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8bff08bf-0035-5f05-9607-493b301e8717" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given Two Perpendicular Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae77e54a-32d3-50f9-90e1-d721c6912eb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057565} {:answer/id #uuid "bef01f32-2af6-504c-9185-33a340c040ed" :answer/